@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@ Note: cultural victory bullets as of now assume 3 legendary cities are required,
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5990+) **Reassign existing AI specialists to a better plot or specialist type:** K-Mod's quick initial estimate could leave a city population member assigned as a specialist even when K-Mod's existing full city-aware comparison rated an available plot or another specialist type higher. The AI now applies that full comparison through an additional pass that can reassign the specialist to the better plot or specialist type (an assignable free-specialist slot (counted by `totalFreeSpecialists()`), which does not use a population member, may change to a better allowed type; fixed-type free specialists (`getFreeSpecialistCount(type)`) remain unchanged, and explicitly AI/DLL-forced specialist assignments are not changed by this pass). This pass only reassigns existing specialists; it never removes a population member from a worked city plot to create a new specialist, preserving the AdvCiv-SAS growth-first safeguards against excessive specialist assignment, and every change must still pass the full city-aware valuation and starvation checks. Compared with the preceding BBAI run without this additional reassignment pass, both measured through turn 402, the new run made 1,963 approved reassignments (918 to plots and 1,045 between specialist types) and reduced remaining logged specialist-origin misses from 2,601 to 0. As a directional sanity check within the new run rather than a before/after comparison, this pass made 201 reassignments from Artist to another job and 46 reassignments to Artist.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5991+) **Reduce one-time corporation-founder pressure on recurring specialist selection:** Before founding a corporation, K-Mod repeatedly used the full value of its headquarters when deciding how strongly cities should favor specialist jobs that generate the required Great Person type. This helps produce the one founder, but a very valuable headquarters could make the AI assign too many of those specialists while waiting for that single Great Person (e.g., if at war but with many artist assignments). The AI now keeps the full value of eventually using the generated Great Person's Join City action, but counts only 50% (by default, tunable) of the corporation's additional value over Join City toward specialist selection. This reduces excessive pre-founder specialist pressure while retaining an incentive to produce the founder, and makes other specialist types or worked plots more competitive without forbidding the required Great Person type. This applies to every Great Person type that can found a corporation, not only Great Artists. Once generated, the Great Person still evaluates founding the corporation at full value. Behavior after the corporation is founded is unchanged. In the BBAI test, this reduced Corporation 7's contribution to Great Artist selection from 31,987 to 18,089; the corporation remained valuable enough that Rome still generated the required Great Artist on turn 297 and founded it on turn 298.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5992+) **Reduce empire-wide specialist pressure from one city's local Join City culture value, especially for Artists (as this specialist gives most culture):** K-Mod uses the best value of having a Great Person Join City anywhere in the empire when weighting every specialist that can generate that Great Person type. BBAI logging showed that one city's high local culture value could therefore make Artists look unusually valuable throughout an empire that was not pursuing cultural victory, including during war: at culture stage 0 with war as its focus, Egypt had 8-9 Artists in Thebes and 7 in Memphis while high Join City culture values elsewhere set its empire-wide Great Artist weight. Outside cultural-victory stages, the AI now counts only 50% of the Join City culture component by default (tunable) when calculating recurring Great Person weights, making other specialist types or worked plots more competitive; all other Join City components keep their full value. The rule checks every Great Person type and reduces any culture its Join City specialist provides, but Great Artists are affected most because their joined specialist provides much more culture. Actual Great Person actions still use full value, and cultural-victory stages 1-4 retain 100% of the culture component. Across directionally comparable but diverging BBAI autoplays, the maximum normalized Great Artist weight fell from 163 to 132 and entries above 130 fell from 111 to 11; the new run still included Join City, Discover, Golden Age, Great Work, and corporation-founding uses of Great Artists.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5993+) **Reduce direct Artist overvaluation in secure, non-cultural AI cities:** After reducing empire-wide Great Artist weight pressure, BBAI diagnostics exposed a narrower local issue: wartime Mediolanum still assigned 5-6 Artists despite having full BFC control, no revolt risk, low culture pressure around 104-105, and an unworked **0 food / 7 hammers / 3 commerce** plot. In AI job comparisons, clean cities now count only 50% of an Artist specialist's direct culture commerce by default (tunable); the Artist's research, Great Person points, and other value remain unchanged. Full Artist culture value is retained for cultural-victory investment, first-ring expansion, occupation/disorder or revolt risk, emergency culture pressure, an insecure city tile, or any unowned, foreign-owned, or culture-contested BFC plot. In the tested autoplay, the 50% rule appeared in 100 secure-city records containing at most 4 Artists, while all 236 records with at least 5 Artists retained 100% because they still had local culture needs; this verifies the deliberately cautious scope rather than proving a controlled overall reduction.
 - Exception to the sanity guards rule, and AI enhancement: if a city hasn’t expanded to its **BFC** yet, auto-assign exactly **one Artist** to pop borders, then stop once secured. Implemented in `CvCity::AI_doTurn`.
 
